# More named calls than the first size of the index that finds a call's
# record by its body: 90 calls in three methods, each bound by name. f(a b) is
# a - b; a call of m gives the sum of j - x for j from 1 to 30: 465 - 30 * x.
# Taken by place, each term is x - j. Entry 7.
fn: f (int: a; int: b) int
    return: a - b
end: f

fn: m1 (int: x) int
    int: r 0
    r: r + f(b: x; a: 1)
    r: r + f(b: x; a: 2)
